  "body": "We do hundreds of thousands of index scans of room_memberships every second, and I'm sure it can't be helpful.\r\n\r\nI think they are coming from queries which join against `current_state_events`, and each event ends up counting as a separate \"index scan\".\r\n\r\nWe also get things like this in the logs:\r\n\r\n```\r\n2018-06-01 16:03:00,514 - synapse.storage.roommember - 87 - INFO - - Fetched room membership for !PVNuPWbpXKukMc....:t2bot.io (75492 users) in 2735 ms\r\n```\r\n\r\nHolding up a db thread for nearly three seconds is not a happy thing to do.\r\n\r\nBasically, I wonder if we should be maintaining a separate table of \"who is in this room right now\", since that's a question we need to ask a lot (and the caches don't help that much as they get invalidated on each membership change).",
